# Every text file checked out and committed with LF endings, whatever the platform
# (package 68; the cold review of 2026-10-22, its 2.3 and R-58: the hotfix's files came back
# CR LF from scripts that wrote them on Windows, and a checkout with core.autocrlf writes CR
# LF too). Git takes the binary files (the chart tiles) by its own test of their content.
# The lines after this one stand over it for their files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose bytes are digested or read whole, kept as committed on every platform: a
# checkout that turned their line endings would move the consent brief's digest (the
# records in docs/agents/consent/ carry it, and the re-ask rule compares it), the
# digests of the briefs kept as test fixtures (tests/test_officer.py pins them: before
# package 37g, before package 42a, and before package 42b), and the checkpoints kept as
# fixtures (gzip). Found at the fold-in of m5c-c, when the Windows job of ci.yml checked
# the fixture out with CR LF.
docs/agents/ConsentBrief.md -text
tests/fixtures/ConsentBrief-before-37g.md -text
tests/fixtures/ConsentBrief-before-42a.md -text
tests/fixtures/ConsentBrief-before-42b.md -text
tests/fixtures/saves/*.checkpoint binary
tests/fixtures/saves/*.json -text

# The records kept as they were filed, their bytes as committed (package 68): the consent
# records (never touched but by the package the specification names), the playtests' saves,
# notes and evidence (some filed with CR LF from the owner's machine), and the first
# brainstorm.
docs/agents/consent/** -text
docs/playtests/** -text
docs/InitialDesignBrainstorm.txt -text
